$CATEGORY: Q17 - Designing Classes

::Q1701::
In Chapter 1, we defined a class as a collection of related methods. 
Now, a class is also a template for a new type of object. {TRUE}

::Q1708::
client - a class that uses objects defined in another class. {TRUE}

::Q1702::
instance - member of a class. Every object is an instance of a class. {TRUE}

::Q1703::
instantiate - create a new instance of a class in the computer's memory. {TRUE}

::Q1704::
instance variable - an attribute of an object; a non-static variable defined at the class level. {TRUE}

::Q1705::
The practice of making instance variables private to limit dependencies between classes. {
    ~ shadowing
    = information hiding
}

::Q1706::
Occurs when a local variable or parameter has the same name as an attribute. {
    = shadowing
    ~ information hiding
}

::Q1707::
A special method that initializes the instance variables of a newly constructed object. {
    ~ getter
    ~ setter
    = constructor
}

::Q1709::
A method that returns the value of an instance variable. {
    = getter
    ~ setter
    ~ constructor
}

::Q1710::
A method that assigns a value to an instance variable. {
    ~ getter
    = setter
    ~ constructor
}

::Q1711::
override - to replace a default implementation of a method, such as toString. {TRUE}

::Q1712::
instance method - a non-static method that has access to this and the instance variables.  {TRUE}

::Q1713::
References to the same object (at the same location in memory) {
    ~ equivalent objects
    = identical objects
}

::Q1714::
Objects that are equal in value, as defined by the equals method. {
    = equivalent objects
    ~ identical objects
}